// Worldgen GPU kernel v1 â€” HLSL port of the CPU reference (hash.h +
// amplifier.cpp), per ADR-0001: single HLSL source compiled to DXIL for UE
// RDG and to SPIR-V (DXC -spirv) for the headless Vulkan determinism/perf
// harness.
//
// DETERMINISM CONTRACT (docs/determinism.md): every expression here must be
// a bit-exact mirror of the CPU reference. Integer-only; int64/uint64
// arithmetic requires Int64 shader ops (D3D12 Int64ShaderOps / Vulkan
// shaderInt64 â€” see ADR-0001). C++ and HLSL agree on two's-complement casts
// and arithmetic >> on signed values. They DO NOT reliably agree on signed
// `/` and `%` when the operands have mixed signs â€” that is undefined in HLSL
// and diverged between AMD and NVIDIA at the M0 gate; see the floorDiv /
// truncDiv comment below and use those helpers instead.
// Any change here that alters output is world-breaking: bump
// vxc::kWorldGenVersion and regenerate goldens, never patch silently.
//
// Kernels:
//   ColumnMain   â€” one thread per column, computes the full ColumnSample
//                  stratigraphy (mirrors vxc::Amplifier::column).
//   VoxelizeMain â€” one thread per column, chained after ColumnMain: reads
//                  that column's GpuColumnSample (NOT recomputed) and fills
//                  a vertical stack of brick-major cell buckets (mirrors
//                  vxc::Amplifier::materialAt / GeneratedWorld<8>::makeBrick).
// Greedy meshing kernels build on this in later ports.

// --- compile target: standalone DXC vs Unreal (G2a) ------------------------
//
// ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH. This file is compiled two ways and the determinism
// gate is only worth anything if both ways compile the SAME text:
//
//   1. standalone DXC (tools/compile-shaders.ps1) -> SPIR-V for the Vulkan
//      bench (voxel-core/bench/gpu_harness.cpp) and DXIL. Resources carry
//      explicit register() slots; the bench's descriptor sets hardcode the
//      -fvk-*-shift mapping of those slots (see the binding map below).
//
//   2. Unreal's shader pipeline (D3D12/SM6), which compiles this file
//      directly as global compute shaders and defines VXC_UE. Unreal binds
//      shader resources by REFLECTED NAME out of a generated parameter
//      struct, and assigns its own register slots -- explicit register()
//      declarations fight that, and a hand-rolled cbuffer collides with the
//      one Unreal generates from the parameter struct.
//
// So the only thing VXC_UE changes is HOW THE SAME RESOURCES ARE DECLARED:
// the names, the types, and every line of arithmetic below are identical.
// The parameter struct on the Unreal side declares the WorldGenParams fields
// as loose parameters with these exact names, so the kernel bodies do not
// know or care which way they were compiled.
//
// VXC_UE is never defined for the bench, so the standalone output is
// unchanged by construction -- verified by recompiling and diffing the SPIR-V
// hashes in shaders/prebuilt/README.md, which must not move.
#ifdef VXC_UE
    #define VXC_REG(slot)
#else
    #define VXC_REG(slot) : register(slot)
#endif

// --- worldgen version lock (Unreal leg only) -------------------------------
//
// The version of vxc::kWorldGenVersion this file is a mirror of. Bump it in
// the SAME commit that re-mirrors the constants below and respins
// shaders/prebuilt -- that is the whole contract this number encodes.
//
// WHY IT IS CHECKED AGAINST THE C++ SIDE. Both of the wrong root causes ever
// published for the determinism gate were version skew wearing a compiler's
// clothes: first "the v8 CPU rules were never mirrored into HLSL" (they were),
// then "DXIL floating-point contraction flipped a layer comparison" (there is
// no floating point in this file). The failure was a CPU worldgen and an HLSL
// worldgen from different versions meeting in one process. A number that both
// sides must agree on turns that from a per-cell mystery into a compile error.
//
// VoxelGpuWorldGen.cpp's ModifyCompilationEnvironment passes
// vxc::kWorldGenVersion in as VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_CPP. Because a define is
// part of the shader's DDC key, bumping either number also forces a recompile
// rather than silently reusing cached bytecode from the previous version.
//
// SCOPE, HONESTLY: vxc::kWorldGenVersion lives in a HEADER (core.h), so this
// catches source-level skew -- an unmirrored kernel -- and NOT a stale
// voxelcore.lib, where fresh headers sit on top of old object code. The
// stale-library case is covered on the C++ side by VoxelEarth.Build.cs's
// timestamp warning and by voxel.GPU.VerifyRegion's pinned CPU-reference
// digest. Two different faults, two different guards.
#define VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_USH 15
#ifdef VXC_UE
    #ifndef VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_CPP
        #error "worldgen.ush compiled under VXC_UE without VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_CPP. Every Unreal-side kernel must derive from FVoxelWorldGenShader so ModifyCompilationEnvironment passes vxc::kWorldGenVersion in."
    #endif
    #if VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_CPP != VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_USH
        #error "worldgen version skew: the linked voxel-core headers and worldgen.ush mirror different worldgen versions. Re-mirror this file from amplifier.cpp/biome.h, bump VXC_WORLDGEN_VERSION_USH, and respin voxel-core/shaders/prebuilt via tools/compile-shaders.ps1."
    #endif
#endif

